diff --git a/packages/corgispec/CHANGELOG.md b/packages/corgispec/CHANGELOG.md
index 7fcd849b64fb4b389c2bc3d50be7899e5e996cc3..fa059a691503a414adb754fb0d3b926682cea1a2 100644
--- a/packages/corgispec/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/packages/corgispec/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,37 @@
 
 All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
 
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Added
+
+- Admit an ordinary pre-Run HEAD advance automatically when the completed Propose handoff still matches the strict-ready
+  source/plan and the advance is proven to lie on the configured integration branch; retain an explicit guarded,
+  idempotent Propose refresh only for deliberate pre-Run retries.
+- Allow only the first current Task Group to use an exact two-parent integration merge, preserving both the planning
+  baseline and configured integration branch ancestry without weakening later per-group commit isolation.
+- Add `ARCHIVE_DELTA_COMPATIBLE` to deterministic readiness so a `MODIFIED` requirement cannot silently omit current
+  canonical scenario identities and fail only during Archive.
+- Add `archive --request-repair --reason <text>` to roll back only reproducible evidence and a pending pre-closeout
+  journal before creating a formal repair successor.
+
+### Changed
+
+- Publish the Apply skill as an implicitly invokable Codex workflow and document the guarded handoff-refresh and
+  first-group integration-merge paths.
+- Make Archive begin consume the same compatibility check through lifecycle readiness, while allowing the repair
+  request to preserve binding and recover a known-bad plan without requiring that plan to pass the new check.
+- Make the Archive skill honor project-local PR/MR integration gates after local closeout: synchronize the exact
+  archive commit while the Run remains `archiving`, and defer tracker closeout, finish, and worktree removal until the
+  guarded finalizer confirms the required merge.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Validate archived acceptance evidence by table-row identity, so narrative QA references do not create false
+  duplicate-criterion findings while missing or genuinely duplicated rows still fail closed.
+- Normalize Git and filesystem paths through their physical locations before RFC ancestry checks, avoiding false
+  outside-repository failures on systems where temporary directories traverse a symlink.
+
 ## [4.0.0-rc2] - 2026-08-19
 
 ### Fixed
